+# Agent notes for tinycalc
+
+tinycalc is a small expression calculator: `tinycalc "2 * (3 + 4)"` prints `14`.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `src/tinycalc/cli.py` is the command-line entry point.
+- `src/tinycalc/evaluate.py` walks the syntax tree and computes the result.
+- Expressions are tokenized and parsed in `src/tinycalc/parser.py`.
+- Tests live in `tests/`, one file per module (`tests/test_evaluate.py`, `tests/test_tokens.py`).
+
+## Commands
+
+```bash
+make install   # editable install into the active virtualenv
+make test      # pytest -q
+make lint      # ruff check src tests
+```
+
+## Before you change something
+
+- Read [the usage guide](docs/usage.md) for the expression grammar.
+- Release steps are in [the release checklist](docs/releasing.md).
+- Keep `pyproject.toml` and `src/tinycalc/__init__.py` at the same version.
